<title>GERMANY: Tietmeyer says Euro must earn stability reputation.</title>
<headline>Tietmeyer says Euro must earn stability reputation.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank President Hans Tietmeyer said on Monday that the future single European currency would not automatically be stable against the dollar and would have to earn its reputation.</p>
<p>&quot;The European central bank must earn this reputation (for stability),&quot; Tietmeyer said in the text of a speech for a reception sponsored by Mercedes-Benz at the IAA truck exhibition in Hanover.</p>
<p>&quot;That can under the circumstances take awhile because credibility can mostly not be built overnight.&quot;</p>
</text>
